======================================================================================================================
    W_raw = 8 pi G N0 L_NN / sqrt(gamma) = (K.K - lambda K^2) + 8 pi G phidot^2/N0^2 + 8 pi G rho_rest u^2/(1-u^2)^(3/2): True
    with the background lapse equation: W = -16*pi*G*V0 - 8*pi*G*mu*(2 - 3*u**2)/(a1*a2*a3*(1 - u**2)**(3/2)) - 2*Lambda  : True;  = CFG294's committed string: True
    k^2 coefficients: F2a alpha - 1/2, physical alpha: True
    V: potential of an OPTIONAL minimally coupled scalar (CFG294's probe); not in the chassis action -> chassis-native V = 0
    rho_rest = mu/sqrt(gamma) = Gamma rho_0 (rest mass per proper khronon-leaf volume); u = a1 v/N0 = speed in the khronon frame (units of c)
  [PASS] C1 W re-derived in-lane from the minisuperspace Lagrangian (anisotropic Bianchi I, dust, homogeneous scalar): W = -2 Lambda - 16 pi G V - 8 pi G rho_rest (2-3u^2)/(1-u^2)^(3/2) after the background lapse equation; k^2 coefficients alpha - 1/2 (F2a) and alpha (physical); identical to CFG294's committed expression
         measured: W True; W_raw True; coefficients True; CFG294 string True; ACTION.md Lambda >= 0 True, no V True
         reading:  V is not a chassis term (ACTION.md has R - 2 Lambda, C-H fields, point masses, Maxwell); the chassis-native W has V = 0 and Lambda >= 0.  The scalar's kinetic energy cancels exactly between W_raw and the background equation

======================================================================================================================
C2  BAROTROPIC PERFECT FLUID (fixed-flux action -N sqrt(gamma) rho(n), J^mu fixed): does pressure enter?
======================================================================================================================
    W_fluid (symbolic, background equation used) = -2 Lambda - 8 pi G B/(1-u^2)^2 with the predicted B: True
    background lapse equation sources E = (rho + p u^2)/(1 - u^2) (khronon-frame energy density): True
    dust limit reproduces C1 (rho_0 = rho_rest sqrt(1-u^2)): True;  u = 0: W = -2 Lambda - 16 pi G rho, pressure absent: True
  [PASS] C2 perfect fluid: W = -2 Lambda - 16 pi G V - 8 pi G B/(1-u^2)^2, B = 2 rho - 3 rho u^2 + p u^2 - 2 p u^4 + (rho+p) c_s^2 u^4 (rho, p fluid-frame; c_s^2 = dp/drho); dust limit = C1; at u = 0 the pressure drops out exactly (W = -2 Lambda - 16 pi G rho)
         measured: form True; E_bg True; dust limit True; u = 0 True
         reading:  pressure enters W only through moving matter (terms O(p u^2)); a fluid at rest in the khronon frame contributes -16 pi G rho whatever its pressure, so a compact star needs no pressure term in the condition

======================================================================================================================
C3  SIGN THEOREMS ON THE MATTER TERM (symbolic)
======================================================================================================================
    (a) dust: B/rho = 2 - 3*X; B > 0 on X in Interval.Ropen(0, 2/3); B = 0 at X = [2/3]
    (b) identity B = 2 rho (1-u^2)^2 + (rho+p) u^2 (1 - (2 - c_s^2) u^2): True;  sampled violations of B >= 2 rho (1-u^2)^2 on {rho >= 0, |p| <= rho, 0 <= c_s^2 <= 1, u^2 <= 1/(2 - c_s^2)}: 0/200000
    (c) dust w=0: B/rho = 2 - 3*X;  roots in [0,1): [2/3] -> u = [0.8165]
    (c) radiation w=1/3: B/rho = -2*(X**2 + 12*X - 9)/9;  roots in [0,1): [-6 + 3*sqrt(5)] -> u = [0.84155]
    (c) stiff w=1: B/rho = -2*(X - 1);  roots in [0,1): [] -> u = []
    (c) w=-1: B/rho = 2*(X - 1)**2;  roots in [0,1): [] -> u = []
  [PASS] C3a dust: for rho > 0 the matter term is negative iff u^2 < 2/3, zero at u^2 = 2/3, positive above
         measured: B/rho = 2 - 3u^2; B > 0 on [0, 2/3)
  [PASS] C3b universal: B = 2 rho (1-u^2)^2 + (rho+p) u^2 (1 - (2 - c_s^2) u^2) identically; so rho >= 0, rho + p >= 0 (null/weak energy condition), c_s^2 >= 0 and u^2 <= 1/(2 - c_s^2) (in particular u^2 <= 1/2 for every fluid) give B >= 2 rho (1-u^2)^2, i.e. a matter term <= -16 pi G rho
         measured: identity True; sampled violations 0/200000 (min excess 2.16e-08)
         reading:  the bound needs only NEC + c_s^2 >= 0; DEC (|p| <= rho) is not used beyond rho + p >= 0
  [PASS] C3c exact thresholds (p = w rho, c_s^2 = w): dust u^2 = 2/3 (u = 0.8165); radiation u^2 = sqrt(45) - 6 (u = 0.8416); stiff w = 1 none (B = 2 rho (1 - u^2)); w = -1 none (B = 2 rho (1-u^2)^2)
         measured: {'dust w=0': [0.816496580927726], 'radiation w=1/3': [0.8415485324681928], 'stiff w=1': [], 'w=-1': []}

======================================================================================================================
C4  THE SIGN CONDITION FOR W (exact, sufficient, strict; chassis-native)
======================================================================================================================
    W = -[2 (Lambda + 8 pi G V) + 8 pi G Sum_i B_i/(1-u_i^2)^2]: True;  W = 0 with no matter at V = -Lambda/(8*pi*G): True
    sufficient: V >= -Lambda/(8 pi G) and every component with rho_i >= 0, rho_i + p_i >= 0, c_s^2 >= 0, u_i below threshold;
    strict:     additionally Lambda + 8 pi G V > 0, or some rho_i > 0 strictly below threshold;
    chassis-native (V = 0, Lambda > 0 observed): W < 0 for every sub-threshold matter content, including vacuum + Lambda.
  [PASS] C4 W <= 0 iff 2(Lambda + 8 pi G V) + 8 pi G Sum B_i/(1-u_i^2)^2 >= 0; sufficient: V >= -Lambda/(8 pi G) and all components sub-threshold with rho >= 0; strict W < 0 if Lambda + 8 pi G V > 0 or some rho_i > 0 sub-threshold; chassis-native (V = 0, Lambda > 0): W < 0 strictly
         measured: exact form True; sign algebra on 20000 samples True; V bound -Lambda/(8 pi G) True
         reading:  Lean (cfg312_lapse_condition_W.lean) certifies the polynomial core of C3a, C3b, C3c(radiation) and C4

